 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Oof, that's tight. You could walk in just as they' starting, or text the couple to ask if you can join from your seat. They usually keep the front row free, and people generally finish their drinks before the couple gets up. Only if you'll be late, and only if it' not the husband's family's turn. They might want to wait. That's the kind of logic weddings need, and it's rare. Good luck!",
